WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.526
Preparation begins with cryptographic inventory.

2
00:00:03.526 --> 00:00:14.825
An inventory records where cryptography is used, including algorithms, protocols, libraries, certificates, keys, systems, services, devices, and dependencies.

3
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:30.211
It should cover external-facing systems, internal service communication, VPNs, SSH, code signing, firmware signing, identity platforms, cloud services, build pipelines, embedded devices, and data protection workflows.

4
00:00:30.211 --> 00:00:39.186
Cryptographic agility is the ability to change algorithms, keys, libraries, and protocols without redesigning the entire system.

5
00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:43.032
Agility is partly technical, but it is also operational.

6
00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:51.366
It requires ownership, documentation, testing, configuration control, vendor engagement, and deployment discipline.

7
00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:58.017
A system that can only use one algorithm forever is fragile, even if that algorithm is strong today.

8
00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:04.508
Post-quantum cryptography provides new algorithms intended to resist known quantum attacks.

9
00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:15.567
During migration, some environments may use hybrid approaches that combine classical and post-quantum mechanisms to manage compatibility and transition risk.

10
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.532
Hybrid designs still need careful testing.

11
00:01:18.532 --> 00:01:29.350
They can affect handshake sizes, certificate sizes, key management, performance, logging, monitoring, and interoperability with older clients or devices.

12
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.914
Vendor questions should be concrete.

13
00:01:31.914 --> 00:01:35.120
Which algorithms and standards are supported?

14
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.043
Which products are in scope?

15
00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:38.566
What timelines apply?

16
00:01:38.566 --> 00:01:40.409
Will updates be validated?

17
00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:43.534
How will certificates, keys, and APIs change?

18
00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:46.018
What testing guidance is available?

19
00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:58.840
A migration roadmap should connect those answers to pilot deployments, compatibility testing, procurement requirements, change windows, rollback plans, and long-term crypto agility.
